WEBVTT

00:00:04.349 --> 00:00:11.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday, 25 November. Are we all on? I've got seven tiles, but one of them might just be frozen.</v>

00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:19.390
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, morning. Can you hear me with this headset? Sounds like I'm stood inside a bucket.</v>

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.120
<v Olumide Adeyemi>We can hear you. Unfortunately, the headset hasn't changed that.</v>

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:33.369
<v Jamie Brennan>Charming. Whose new car's that in the car park, then? Grey one, taking up about a space and a half.</v>

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:37.719
<v David Whitfield>Not mine. Mine's the one with more primer than paint.</v>

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.770
<v Callum Reid>Grey one probably costs more than my house. Anyway, morning.</v>

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:48.049
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get onto vehicle valuations, what's already finished? Keep that separate from the actions.</v>

00:00:50.429 --> 00:00:57.079
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, already swapped the filter on the site water yesterday. That's done, not something we're carrying into today.</v>

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.100
<v David Whitfield>That was the one we had on yesterday's list, yeah?</v>

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.840
<v Callum Reid>That's it. Same one. Closed off.</v>

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:12.209
<v Sarah Okafor>And I tested the line one HPU yesterday and it's all fine now. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:18.609
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Good. No outstanding controls bit on that, then. I'm not adding anything.</v>

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:26.079
<v Sarah Okafor>One observation: I heard a slight rattle from the line three. Nothing to action yet, just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:30.859
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, so that's not a maintenance job coming out of this?</v>

00:01:32.709 --> 00:01:36.209
<v Sarah Okafor>No, just an observation at this point. No new action.</v>

00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:42.420
<v Jamie Brennan>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the big board. Still blocked, I'm afraid.</v>

00:01:44.879 --> 00:01:48.730
<v Fiona Doyle>So there's still no confirmed delivery slot. Same position as before.</v>

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:57.310
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Nothing new to promise this morning. That isn't a fresh chasing job, just the blocker as it stands.</v>

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:08.330
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Separately, I'll go to the overflow store to pick up the replacement parts for the GT2 inlet valve first thing tomorrow. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:14.710
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, separate from the big board delivery. Don't want those two getting muddled together.</v>

00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:21.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. Mine's the pickup from the overflow store, not waiting on that supplier confirmation.</v>

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.379
<v Callum Reid>Got you, Sarah. First thing tomorrow for the GT2 inlet valve parts.</v>

00:02:27.669 --> 00:02:32.919
<v Sarah Okafor>Doyler, can you do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances this morning? Top priority please.</v>

00:02:33.689 --> 00:02:38.590
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances this morning. Top priority, understood.</v>

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.000
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, talking over you—pre-use checks, rather than anything wider on them?</v>

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.770
<v Fiona Doyle>That's right, the pre-use checks. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:54.710
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll check the guarding on the arm on two by 11am. Normal priority, that one.</v>

00:02:56.659 --> 00:03:01.210
<v David Whitfield>The guarding specifically, yeah? Not a general mechanical inspection of the whole arm.</v>

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:08.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, specifically the guarding on the arm on two. Keeping it to that, by 11am.</v>

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:12.180
<v Callum Reid>Fine, Sarah. Normal priority for that check, understood.</v>

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:18.259
<v Jamie Brennan>Speaking of keeping things contained, anyone actually risking outdoor plans this weekend?</v>

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.919
<v Tomasz Nowak>Have you seen the forecast? Sideways rain. Very scenic.</v>

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:30.060
<v Jamie Brennan>We'd said we'd go for a walk. Think the weather's going to turn that into sitting in a café, honestly.</v>

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:35.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Solid British weekend. Right, back to it—two separate things here, don't bundle them together.</v>

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:43.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you update the risk assessment for work on the water booster by Wednesday? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:46.009 --> 00:03:51.259
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, by Wednesday as in today, just so we're not reading that as next week?</v>

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:59.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, today, Wednesday. It matters but it's not urgent; it doesn't jump ahead of the top-priority stuff.</v>

00:04:00.629 --> 00:04:05.530
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. I'll update the risk assessment for work on the water booster by Wednesday.</v>

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:13.039
<v David Whitfield>That's the paperwork for the work, not an instruction to start work on the water booster itself?</v>

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:19.259
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. Risk assessment update only. I'm not taking on a separate booster job here.</v>

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:30.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Then, Tomasz, can you book a contractor to look at the front end of one by the end of the week? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:39.160
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. The booking by the end of the week, rather than saying they'll definitely have been on site by then?</v>

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:46.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Book a contractor to look at it. We're not promising their attendance by the end of the week.</v>

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:56.980
<v Tomasz Nowak>Okay, I'll book a contractor to look at the front end of one by the end of the week. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—got it.</v>

00:04:57.339 --> 00:05:01.540
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Right, so we're not turning that into an in-house strip-down as well.</v>

00:05:04.029 --> 00:05:07.879
<v Sarah Okafor>No. Just the contractor booking. Let's not grow legs on it.</v>

00:05:08.959 --> 00:05:15.259
<v Fiona Doyle>Before I forget, there's a birthday cake in the office. That's information, not another item for your list.</v>

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.110
<v Jamie Brennan>Depends what sort of cake. Might be the most important information we've had.</v>

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:25.389
<v Fiona Doyle>Chocolate. Already cut, too, so nobody needs an engineering drawing.</v>

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:31.050
<v Callum Reid>Still get someone arguing about the tolerances on the slices.</v>

00:05:32.959 --> 00:05:36.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Without a doubt. Anything else that actually needs to be agreed?</v>

00:05:38.009 --> 00:05:46.060
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, one from me. I'll write up the near miss at the long belt at half two. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:05:46.769 --> 00:05:50.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fiona Doyle. At half two, specifically—not just sometime this afternoon?</v>

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:56.680
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly, at half two. I'll drop everything for that one and do the write-up then.</v>

00:05:58.149 --> 00:06:03.050
<v Callum Reid>Right. The write-up of the near miss we've already discussed, not a second incident?</v>

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:09.449
<v Fiona Doyle>Same near miss at the long belt, yes. Just making the write-up an agreed action.</v>

00:06:11.519 --> 00:06:17.120
<v Jamie Brennan>Is that rain on someone's microphone, or have we got a crisp packet joining the call?</v>

00:06:18.439 --> 00:06:23.339
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Headset cable rubbing on my jacket. Teams makes it sound like a bearing failure.</v>

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.449
<v David Whitfield>Most convincing bit of audio we've had all morning.</v>

00:06:29.459 --> 00:06:38.209
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, six actions agreed. The big board is still blocked, the finished jobs stay finished, and the rattle is only an observation. Nothing else added.</v>

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:41.069
<v Callum Reid>All clear from me. Cheers, everyone.</v>

00:06:43.329 --> 00:06:45.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks all. That's us. Bye.</v>
